  "application_type_full": "Householder planning permission",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: Unnumbered Pre-Existing Plans, Unnumbered Existing Plans. Received: 04 August 2026.\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - The detached single storey outbuilding hereby permitted shall only be used for a purpose incidental to the enjoyment of the house at the 'Site Address' described at the top of this decision letter and for no other purpose (for example, it may not be used as a self-contained dwelling or contain a bedroom, bathroom, kitchen or other primary residential accommodation, nor may it be used for business purposes). \r\nReason: In order to protect neighbours' living conditions and the character of the area.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - Within 3 months of the date of this decision, the bathroom and kitchen facilities within the outbuilding hereby approved shall be permanently removed in their entirety in accordance with the approved drawings. Written confirmation shall be submitted to the Local Planning Authority within the 3-month period, supported by dated photographic evidence clearly demonstrating the removal of the bathroom and kitchen facilities.\r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the outbuilding remains ancillary to the main dwelling and does not form a separate independent unit of residential accommodation, safeguarding the character and appearance of the site and surrounding neighbours\r\n"
  ],
